[
    {
        "content": "<p>I am trying to do one of the exercises in <em>Mathematics in Lean</em>, and I am puzzled by the following. This is the MWE:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Data</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Real</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Basic</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">namespace</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C03S06</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ConvergesTo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ε</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∃</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≥</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">N</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">n</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ε</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">convergesTo_unique</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">sa</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ConvergesTo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">sb</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ConvergesTo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">by_contra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">abne</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">abs_pos</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>For some reason, <code>abs_pos</code> says:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Tactic</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"ss\">`rewrite</span><span class=\"bp\">`</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">failed</span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Did</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">not</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">find</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">an</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">occurrence</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">of</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">pattern</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|?</span><span class=\"n\">m</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"m\">26</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span>\n<span class=\"k\">in</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">the</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">target</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">expression</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Why does this happen? The pattern is clearly there (?)</p>",
        "id": 612539354,
        "sender_full_name": "Eduardo de Lorenzo Poza",
        "timestamp": 1784886503
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>it is there but also is not, the order matters, if you use this you get to the next subgoal for instance:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&lt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">abs_pos</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Or if you want your original</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rw</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">gt_iff_lt</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"n\">abs_pos</span><span class=\"o\">]</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 612540684,
        "sender_full_name": "Yan Yablonovskiy 🇺🇦",
        "timestamp": 1784887020
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>it's because <code>0&lt;....</code> is not the same as <code>`....&gt;0</code><br>\ntry this :</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">theorem</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">convergesTo_unique</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℕ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ℝ</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">      </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">sa</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ConvergesTo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">sb</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">ConvergesTo</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">by_contra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">abne</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"k\">have</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"n\">a</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">-</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">b</span><span class=\"bp\">|</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">abs_sub_pos</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mpr</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">abne</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"gr\">sorry</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 612541353,
        "sender_full_name": "Alfredo Moreira-Rosa",
        "timestamp": 1784887240
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"942100\">Alfredo Moreira-Rosa</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/pattern.20matching/near/612541353\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>it's because <code>0&lt;....</code> is not the same as <code>`....&gt;0</code><br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>To be slightly nit picking, it is not syntactically the same, but mathematically it is the same. </p>\n<p>I think that's the key distinction to explicitly state just in case, as it's lack may be leading to expecting it to work in the first place.</p>",
        "id": 612541592,
        "sender_full_name": "Yan Yablonovskiy 🇺🇦",
        "timestamp": 1784887320
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Another hint, when trying to find a proof. you have discovery tactics for these simple cases :</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>exact?</code> : that will find an exact proof of your goal</li>\n<li><code>hint</code> : that will try different tactics to find a proof (will be replaced by <code>try?</code>)</li>\n<li><code>try?</code> : that will use hammer tactics to find a proof (don't give same results as hint currently)</li>\n<li><code>apply?</code> : will propose many partial proof that advance the goal</li>\n</ul>\n<p>There is a lot more, but for simple use cases these are great.</p>",
        "id": 612543456,
        "sender_full_name": "Alfredo Moreira-Rosa",
        "timestamp": 1784888009
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thanks to both of you! I thought <code>a &lt; b</code> and <code>b &gt; a</code> were (syntactically) the same, since <code>a ≤ b</code> and <code>b ≥ a</code> are definitionally the same.</p>",
        "id": 612543770,
        "sender_full_name": "Eduardo de Lorenzo Poza",
        "timestamp": 1784888156
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>No definitional is weaker, syntactically eq -&gt; definitionally eq, definitionally eq -/-&gt; syntactically.</p>\n<p>And really propositionally equal will be one of the more important categories to talk about, weaker than them both.</p>\n<p>Using <code>rw</code> is part of metaprogramming under the hood, so there may lie some confusion there. </p>\n<p>In particular, in the \"math doing\" parts, equality is largely done on the propositional layer. </p>\n<p>But, on the meta layer(abuse of notation here with reusing layer in a different way, sorry) , syntactical equality does become more important, and thats  partly the layer <code>rw</code> is looking at when it complains to you about this \"ambiguity\".</p>\n<p>Syntactic is extremely strict and literal , its \"almost\" essentially saying those characters / strings are identical, not delving into any real meaning yet.</p>\n<p>\"Almost\" partly because even some of the prior discussion is strictly wrong, verbatim and thus without annotations on the types, those are not actually able to be analysed syntactically (or without the full context I guess, but I think that would involve inferring some stuff still before you can even ask if two expressions are syntactically equal). But such nuance is not key here.</p>\n<p>This \"ambiguity\" is also more part of the learning journey though, in reality and over time, especially if you delve into metaprogramming, you would abstract over this with stronger tactics that can indeed see these two as equal.</p>",
        "id": 612544564,
        "sender_full_name": "Yan Yablonovskiy 🇺🇦",
        "timestamp": 1784888438
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Note also its even dangerous to say <code>a ≤ b</code> and <code>b ≥ a</code> are definitionally equal. </p>\n<p>That is <code>a = b ∨ a &lt; b</code> and <code>b = a ∨ b &gt; a</code> say (the actual definition is not this but the same line of thinking will hold),  I don't believe these are definitionally equal, in that they do not reduce/eval to the same expression by default. But they are provably, i.e, propositionally equal, via \"induction\" ( a funny word to try interpret in the usual sense here, but its more in the \"inductive type\" sense ).</p>",
        "id": 612557228,
        "sender_full_name": "Yan Yablonovskiy 🇺🇦",
        "timestamp": 1784893168
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><code>a ≥ b</code> is defined to mean <code>b ≤ a</code>, see <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=GE.ge#doc\">docs#GE.ge</a></p>",
        "id": 612558421,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1784893577
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"816344\">Aaron Liu</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/113489-new-members/topic/pattern.20matching/near/612558421\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p><code>a ≥ b</code> is defined to mean <code>b ≤ a</code>, see <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=GE.ge#doc\">docs#GE.ge</a></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Yea comment was primarily conceptually aimed, I edited after the initial post to further clarify.</p>\n<p>As an expert, do you have anything you maybe also want to add here though? I do not claim expert hood and happy to learn and be taught things, as I assume all of us in this section are.</p>",
        "id": 612559036,
        "sender_full_name": "Yan Yablonovskiy 🇺🇦",
        "timestamp": 1784893776
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>oh that's not how I read that</p>",
        "id": 612559818,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1784894053
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I do have something to add though</p>",
        "id": 612560152,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1784894193
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>because <code>a &lt; b</code> and <code>b &gt; a</code> are not syntactically equal, mathlib prefers to (almost) always write theorems in terms of <code>a &lt; b</code>, so generally it will be harder to work with <code>b &gt; a</code> statements</p>",
        "id": 612560458,
        "sender_full_name": "Aaron Liu",
        "timestamp": 1784894306
    }
]